  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 158 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe daily chances of showers and storms is certainly still on the \ntable as the high retrogrades west back toward the southern high \nplains, but looks to be more amplified and that would give a better \nchance at drawing up more Gulf moisture and eastern Pacific moisture \nthat has been over the NM area to our area.  Still low confidence at \nthis time, as models continue to keep a ridge over the Panhandles, \nbut struggle with the strength and overall position of the ridge \nmoving into the extended. Now as we head into next week, we're \nseeing that the ridge is breaking down but still expands back to the \neast and still keeps most of the moisture running up and over the \nPanhandles, but there are subtle hints that we could get some of \nthat moisture clip the northwest.  \n\nWeber",
